# /hi/<name> is a person's own address. Cloudflare Pages has no file at that path, so this rewrites
# it - status 200, not a redirect - onto /hi/ with the name as a parameter. The address in the bar
# never changes, which is the whole point of a name people say out loud.
#
# ONE RULE, ON PURPOSE. Jessie, 2026-09-19: the long-term goal is that this moves to appear.network
# "with the press of a button on the domain at one point". So nothing anywhere stores a finished
# address - the sheet holds the NAME and only this line and one helper know what it turns into.
/hi/*  /hi/index.html?name=:splat  200
